**How to implement.** Choosing a kit opens it, bumps the history and hands it to the window; a question an open raises becomes an offer (001 §F 'New kit…: choose or create a folder. An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them'; 'Open kit…: a folder without .kit-json offers Make this a kit'; 'Choosing a kit opens the constructor in that mode'; 001 §E 'an open read-only choice'; 001 §P CreateKit, OpenKit; the S5.2 brief: choosing a kit bumps the history and opens the constructor window in the mode the screen was opened for; step 169: `KitHistory.bump` takes the limit, the clock, the folder and the kit file). In `KitStartView.fs` (step 176), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) `KitStartMsg` gains `CreateKit of KitFolder` (New kit… and Make this a kit), `OpenKit of KitFolder` (Open kit… and a history row), `OpenKitReadOnly of KitFolder` (the read-only offer's Open read-only, and how a test opens a committed kit, .spec-md §3.12), `DismissKitStartOffer` (an offer's Cancel) and `KitOpenFailed of KitLibraryError` (the window reports a kit whose resolution failed, step 179). (2) `updateKitStart`: `CreateKit folder` answers through `KitOpening.openKitAt folder ReadWriteKitAccess m.context.clock m.context.author m.context.imports` (step 150: a folder that holds no kit is initialised keeping every file it holds, a kit is opened); `OpenKit folder` through `KitOpening.openExistingKitAt folder m.context.clock m.context.imports` (step 172); `OpenKitReadOnly folder` through `openKitAt folder ReadOnlyKitAccess …`, which writes nothing to the kit. One private function of the folder, the answer and the model reads every answer, in this order. `Ok opened` bumps the history through `m.context.kitHistory.changeHistory (fun h -> h.bump m.context.limit m.context.clock folder opened.library.kit.kitFile)` (steps 169, 171), then calls `m.context.showKit opened` once, and answers no offer, the bumped history and its rows, and no status; when the bump answers `Error e` the kit is still handed over and `status` is `e.notSavedCaption`. `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder))` answers `ReadOnlyKitOffer (folder, holder)` and no status; `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _))` answers `MakeKitOffer folder` and no status; any other `Error e` answers `NoKitStartOffer` and `status` `e.openFailedCaption` (step 173). An error hands nothing over and bumps nothing. `DismissKitStartOffer` answers `NoKitStartOffer`, writing nothing, and `KitOpenFailed e` answers `NoKitStartOffer` and `status` `e.openFailedCaption`. A read-only open bumps the history too, because the user chose the kit. No retry, cache, confirmation or other message is added. Tests, in `KitStartTests` (step 176), over folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "KitStartTests", <a new GUID>)` and an in-memory history whose present folders are the fact's folders; every kit the fixture's `showKit` recorded, and every kit a fact holds open itself, is closed at its end. `New kit initialises an empty folder, bumps the history and hands the kit over`: `CreateKit` of a folder named `Optics QZ` that does not exist records one shown kit, read-write, whose kit file is named `Optics QZ`; the folder holds `.kit-json`, `data` and `library`; the store's history holds one unstarred entry of that folder with the kit's id and name, opened at the clock's last answer; the rows list it; and no offer or status remains. `Open kit opens an existing kit and bumps it above the others`: over a history holding an older entry of another folder, `OpenKit` of a kit made by `openKitAt` and closed records one shown read-write kit, and the history's first entry is that kit's folder. `Open kit on a folder that is not a kit offers Make this a kit, and accepting it keeps the folder's files`: `OpenKit` of a folder holding `notes.txt` records nothing and answers `MakeKitOffer` of it, the folder still holding exactly `notes.txt`; `CreateKit` of it then records one shown kit, the folder holds `.kit-json`, `data`, `library` and `notes.txt`, and no offer remains; over a second such folder `DismissKitStartOffer` answers no offer and the folder still holds exactly `notes.txt`. `a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only, which opens it and writes nothing to the kit`: with the kit held open by an `openKitAt` of the fact, `OpenKit` records nothing and answers `ReadOnlyKitOffer` whose holder names this process; `OpenKitReadOnly` then records one shown kit whose context is read-only, every file of the folder keeps its bytes, and the history's first entry is the folder. `a kit that cannot be opened is shown and nothing is handed over or bumped`: a kit whose `E1.experiment-json` the test writes as `{` makes `OpenKit` record nothing, answer no offer and a status naming `E1.experiment-json`, leave the history unchanged and hold no `.oc/lock`. `a failed resolution reported by the window is shown`: `KitOpenFailed (KitLibraryKitErr (KitIoErr "lost"))` over a model holding a `MakeKitOffer` answers no offer and a status containing `lost`.

**Acceptance.** After the open messages land, CreateKit MUST initialise or open a folder, OpenKit MUST open only a kit and offer Make this a kit for any other folder, a kit open elsewhere MUST be offered read-only, and every successful open MUST bump the history and hand the kit to `showKit` once while a failure hands nothing over; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `New kit initialises an empty folder, bumps the history and hands the kit over`, `Open kit opens an existing kit and bumps it above the others`, `Open kit on a folder that is not a kit offers Make this a kit, and accepting it keeps the folder's files`, `a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only, which opens it and writes nothing to the kit`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown and nothing is handed over or bumped` and `a failed resolution reported by the window is shown`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
